Spec: SpecDD Reference Warning Annotator

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Report unresolved SpecDD path, glob, and explicit symbol candidates as editor warnings.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDPathAnnotator.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDPathAnnotator.kt

Can read:
  ./SpecDDPathReferenceExtractor.kt
  ./SpecDDPathResolver.kt
  ./SpecDDSymbolReferenceExtractor.kt
  ./SpecDDSymbolReference.kt
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/SpecDDFileType.kt
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/references/SpecDDPathAnnotatorBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Extend IntelliJ `@Annotator`.
  Annotate only SpecDD files.
  Report warning annotations for unresolved path, glob, and explicit symbol candidates.
  Report unresolved explicit paths wherever explicit paths are recognized.
  Report unresolved explicit symbols wherever explicit symbols are recognized.
  Ignore comments, blank lines, section headers, escaped `@`, embedded `@`, URLs, and unprefixed prose.
  Attach create-path quick fixes to unresolved exact path candidates.
  Do not attach create-path quick fixes to unresolved glob candidates.
  Do not attach quick fixes to unresolved symbol candidates.
  Do not report errors.
  Ignore prose-like unresolved candidates without path syntax.
  Keep warnings separate from structural validation diagnostics.

Must not:
  Define structural validation rules.
  Define syntax highlighting colors.
